G2106.def:
εὐ-δοκέω, -ῶ
(on the derivation, see EL, § 28, 6) [in LXX chiefly for רָצָה, also for אָבָה, חָפֵץ, etc. ;] 
__1. with inf. (Polyb., al.), to be well pleased, to think it good, to give consent (so frequently in π. in legal docu­ments; Milligan, Th., 22 f.): Luc 12:32, Romains 15:26-27, 1 Corinthiens 1:21, Galates 1:15, Colossiens 1:19, R, mg. (ICC, in l, but see infr.), 1 Thessaloniciens 2:8 3:1; μᾶλλον εὐ., 2 Corinthiens 5:8; with accusative and inf. (Polyb., i, 8, 4), Col, l.with, R, txt. (Lft., in l). 
__2. to be well pleased or take pleasure with or in a person or thing; 
__(a) with dative (Polyb., al.; 1Ma.1:43, I Esther 4:39): 2 Thessaloniciens 2:12; 
__(b) as frequently in LXX, 
__α with accusative: Matthieu 12:13, Hébreux 10:5, 8" (LXX) ; 
__β before ἐν (cf. Heb. בּ רָצָה, Psaumes 149:4): Matthieu 3:17 17:5, Marc 1:11, Luc 3:22 (on the tense, see M, Pr., 134 f.; DCG, i,308 b), 1 Corinthiens 10:5, 2 Corinthiens 12:10, Hébreux 10:38" (LXX) ; 
__(with) before εἰς: 2 Pierre 1:17. (cf. συν-ευδοκέω, and see Cremer, 213 f.; Field, Notes, 48 f.; DCG, i, 355a.)†

G2128.def:
εὐλογητός, -όν
(εὐλογέω), [in LXX chiefly for בָּרַךְ ;] 
blessed; 
__(a) of men (Genèse 12:2 A, Deutéronome 7:14, Juges 17:2 B, Ruth 2:20, 1 Rois 15:13); 
__(b) of God (Lft., Notes, 310 f.), as chiefly in LXX (Genèse 9:26, Exode 17:10, Psaumes 18:46, al.): Luc 1:68, Romains 1:25 9:5 (ICC, in l), 2 Corinthiens 1:3 11:31, Éphésiens 1:3, 1 Pierre 1:3; absol., ὁ εὐλογητός (Dalman, Words, 200; JThS, v, 453), Marc 14:61 (Cremer, 769).†

G2186.def:
ἐφ-ίστημι 
[in LXX for נָצַב ni., שִׁית, נָתַן, etc. ;] 
__1. causal in pres., impf., fut., 1 aor., to set upon or by, set up, etc. (Æsch., Hdt., Arist., al). 
__2. Intrans. in mid, and in pf. and 2 aor. act.; 
__(a) to stand upon; 
__(b) to be set over; 
__(with) to stand by, be present, be at hand, come on or upon: Luc 2:38 10:40 20:1, Actes 6:12 12:7 22:13, 20 23:27, 2 Timothée 4:2; with dative pars., Luc 2:9 24:4, Actes 4:1 23:11; with dative bc., Actes 17:5; before έπί, with accusative, Actes 10:17 11:11; of rain, Actes 28:2; of evils impending, with dative of person(s), 1 Thessaloniciens 5:3; before έπί (Wis.6:9), Luc 21:34; of time, 2 Timothée 4:6 (cf. κατ-, συν-εφίστημι).†

G2192.def:
ἔχω, 
[in LXX for אָצֵל (ἐχόμενος), יֵשׁ,בַּעַל, etc., 59 words in all ;] 
(on the Aktionsart of the various tenses, see M, Pr., 110, 145, 150, 183), to have, as in cl., in various senses and constructions. 
__I. Trans.; 
__1. 1. to have, hold, hold fast, etc.; 
__(a) to hold, as, in the hand: Apocalypse 5:8 14:6, al.; ἐν τ. χειρί, Apocalypse 1:16 10:2, al.; 
__(b) of arms and clothing, = φέρω, φορέω, to bear, wear: Matthieu 3:4 22:12, al.; so frequently present ptcp. (LS, see word, A, I, 6; Bl., 74, 2), Marc 11:13, Jean 18:10, Apocalypse 9:17, al.; 
__(with) of a woman, ἐν γαστρὶ ἔ, to be with child: Marc 13:17, Romains 9:10; 
__(d) to hold fast, keep: Luc 19:20; metaphorically, of the mind and conduct, Marc 16:8 (cf. Job 21:6, Ésaïe 13:8; Deiss., BS, 293; Field, Notes, 44f.), Jean 14:21, Romains 1:28, 1 Timothée 3:9, 2 Timothée 1:13, Apocalypse 6:9, al.; 
__(e) to involve: Hébreux 10:35 (LXX), Jacques 1:4, 1 Jean 4:18; (f) = Lat. habere (Bl., §34, 5; 73, 5), to hold, consider: with accusative and predic. ptcp., Luc 14:18; with accusative, before ὡς, Matthieu 14:5; εἰς (Hebraism), Matthieu 21:46; on (Bl., §70, 2), Marc 11:32. 
__2. to have, possess; 
__(a) in general, with accusative of thing(s): Matthieu 19:22, Marc 10:22, Luc 12:19, Jean 10:16, 1 Corinthiens 11:22, al.; of wealth or poverty, absol., ἔχειν (neg. οὐκ, μή), Matthieu 13:12 25:29, 2 Corinthiens 8:12; ἐκ τ. ἔχειν, according to your means, 2 Corinthiens 8:11; 
__(b) of relationship, association, and: πατέρα, Jean 8:41; γυναῖκα (MM, xiv), 1 Corinthiens 7:2; φίλον, Luc 11:5; βασιλέα, Jean 19:15; ποιμένα, Matthieu 9:36; with dupl. accusative, Matthieu 3:9, al.; 
__(with) of parts or members: ὦτα, Matthieu 19:15; μέλη, Romains 12:4; θεμελίους, 
__(d) with accusative, as periphrasis of verb: μνεῖαν ἔ. (= μεμνῆσθαι), 1 Thessaloniciens 3:6; ἀγάπην, Jean 13:35; γνῶσιν, 1 Corinthiens 8:1; πεποίθησιν, 2 Corinthiens 3:4; θλίψιν, Jean 16:33, etc. (Thayer, see word, I, 2, f., g.); 
__(e) of duty, necessity, etc.: ἀνάγκην, 1 Corinthiens 7:37; νόμον, Jean 19:7; ἐπιταγήν, 1 Corinthiens 7:25; ἀγῶνα, Philippiens 1:30; κρίμα, 1 Timothée 5:12; 
__(f) of complaints and disputes; κατά, with genitive of person(s), Matthieu 5:23, Marc 11:25; id. before ὅτι, Apocalypse 2:4, 20; with accusative before πρός, Actes 24:19, al.; 
__(g) with inf., 
__(α) (cl.) to be able (Field, Notes, 14): Matthieu 18:25, Marc 14:8 (sc. ποιῆσαι), Luc 12:4, Actes 4:14, al; 
__(β) of necessity (BL, §69, 4): Luc 12:50, Actes 23:17-19 28:19.
__II. Intrans. (BL, §53, 1), to be in a certain condition: ἑτοίμως ἔ., with inf., Actes 21:13, 2 Corinthiens 12:14; ἐσχάτως (which see), Marc 5:23; κακῶς, to be ill, Matthieu 4:24, al.; καλῶς, Mk 16:[18]; κομψότερον, Jean 4:52; πῶς, Actes 15:36; impers., ἄλλως εἴχει, it is otherwise, 1 Timothée 5:25; οὕτως, Actes 7:1, al.; τὸ νῦν ἔχον, as things now are (Tob.7:11), Actes 24:25. 
__III. Mid., -ομαι, to hold oneself fast, hold on or cling to, be next to: with genitive, τ. ἐχόμενα σωτηρίας, Hébreux 6:9 (Rendall, in l.); ptcp., ὁ ἐχόμενος, near, next: of place, Marc 1:38; of time, τ. ἐχομένη (ἡμέρα, expressed or understood), Luc 13:33, Actes 20:15 21:26; (σαββάτῳ), Actes 13:44. (Cf. ἀν-, προσ-αν-, ἀντ-, ἀπ-, ἐν-, ἐπ-, κατ-, μετ-, παρ-, περι-, προ-, προσ-, συν-, ὑπερ-, ὑπ-έχω.)

G2193.def:
ἕως, 
relative particle (Lat. donee, usque), 
expressing the terminus ad quem (cf. Burton, §321ff.). 
__I. As conjunction; 
__1. till, until; 
__(a) of a fact in past time, with indic.: Matthieu 2:9, al. (Wis.10:14, al.); 
__(b) ἕως ἄν, with subjc. aor.: Matthieu 2:13 5:18, Marc 6:10, al.; without ἄν (M. Pr., 168f.; Lft., Notes, 115), Marc 14:32 (Burton, §325), Luc 12:59, 2 Thessaloniciens 2:7, al.; 
__(with) with indic., present (Burton, §328; BL, §65, 10): Marc 6:45, Jean 21:22, 23 1 Timothée 4:13. 
__2. C. indic., as long as, while (Burton, §327): Jean 9:4 (Plat., Phaedo, 89c). 
__II. As an adverb (chiefly in late writers). 
__1. Of time, until, unto; 
__(a) as prep. with genitive (BL, §40, 6; M, Pr., 99): τ. ἡμέρας, Matthieu 26:29, Luc 1:80, Romains 11:8, al.; ὥρας, Matthieu 27:45, al.; τέλους, 1 Corinthiens 1:8, 2 Corinthiens 1:13; τ. νῦν, Matthieu 24:21, Marc 13:19 (1Ma.2:33); ἐτῶν ὀγ. (Field, Notes, 49f.), Luc 2:37; τ. ἐλθεῖν, Actes 8:40; before names and events, Matthieu 1:17 2:15, Luc 11:51, Jacques 5:7, al.; 
__(b) before οὗ, ὅτου, with the force of a conjc. (Burton, §330; M, Pr., 91); 
__(α) ἕ. οὗ (Hdt., ii, 143; Plut., al.): with indic., Matthieu 1:25 (WH br., οὗ) 13:33, al.; with subjc. aor., Matthieu 14:22, al.; 
__(β) ἔ. ὅτου: with subjc., Luc 13:8; with indic., Matthieu 5:25 (until), Jean 9:18; 
__(with) with adv. (ἔ. ὀψέ, Thuc, iii, 108): ἄρτι, Matthieu 11:12, Jean 2:10, 1 Corinthiens 4:13, al.; πότε (M, Pr., 107), Matthieu 17:17, Marc 9:19, Jean 10:24, al. 
__2. Of place, as far as, even to, unto (Arist., al.); 
__(a) as prep. with genitive (see supr.): Mt 1123, Lk 1015, al.; 
__(b) with adv. (BL, §40, 6): ἄνω, Jean 2:7; ἔσω, Marc 14:54; κάτω, Matthieu 27:51, Marc 15:38; ὧδε, Luc 23:5; 
__(with) with prep.: ἔξω, Actes 21:5; πρός, Luc 24:50 (Field, Notes, 83). 
__3. Of quantity, measure, etc.: Matthieu 18:21, Marc 6:23, Luc 22:51, al.

G2197G.def:
Ζαχαρίας, -ου, ὁ (Heb. זַכַּי); 
__1. Zacharias, father of John the Baptist: Luc 1:5, 12-13 1:18, 21 1:40, 59 1:67 3:2. 
__2. Zechariah, the son of Jehoiada (in txt. wrongly called son of Barachiah; cf. 2 Chroniques 24:19 ff.): Matthieu 23:35, Luc 11:51.†

